reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: How does the standard tell projects about hook template changes without overwriting their copies?

Records the decision that project-owned hook copies are diagnosed via two hashes in .engsys/hooks.txt and updated only explicitly (hooks update, --force, --adopt).
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; the five states, update rules and the four rejected alternatives are preserved in order.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences.
State names (current, owned, outdated, modified, missing), commands and paths kept verbatim; no Korean literals retained.
The incident where upgrade overwrote this repository's pre-push during implementation is kept as stated, without added detail.

